# Response headers for the static build. Cloudflare Workers static assets read this
# file from the uploaded directory (`wrangler.jsonc`); it is parsed by the platform,
# never served as an asset.
#
# Astro fingerprints the generated bundles under /_assets/, so their content can
# never change under a given name: they are the "hashed assets are cached for a
# long time" half of doc/DESIGN.md, 安全与可复现性.
#
# Nothing else is set here on purpose. HTML and /pyodide/ keep Cloudflare's default
# `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` plus ETag: the runtime files are self-hosted
# under stable names, and a Pyodide version bump replaces their bytes in place, so
# a long-lived cache entry would pin a reader to a stale interpreter.

/_assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31556952, immutable
